{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The ostrich (בת היענה).</b> Some say it is a species in which no males are found, like the hare (ארנבת). And the word כיענים is no objection, for they are not males; rather they are females, like יעלים and רחלים." "<b>And the תחמס.</b> From the root of חמס." "<b>And the שחף.</b> It produces שחפת." "<b>And the נץ.</b> It has much plumage. And the probable interpretation is that it is the known one that spreads its wings constantly toward the south, for it seeks a warm place."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:26.489514862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}